Tao et al. 2019
    Statistical structure of locomotion (v||, v-perp HMM/HHMM). In the
    standard library, the fly tracks fit that observation model and use
    it to shape the bridge that closes each recorded track back to its
    first sample, and the fictional fly tracks the cyber look draws are
    generated from the same per-animal fit; this is not a MATLAB port.
    eLife 8:e41235. doi:10.7554/eLife.41235
    https://elifesciences.org/articles/41235
    https://github.com/bhandawat/HHMM (GPL-3.0)

Dommanget-Kott et al. 2024
    Hidden Markov model of zebrafish locomotion. The fish tracks cite this
    and close on the same standard-library bridge as the flies. The
    fictional fish tracks are generated by the same observation model as
    the fictional flies, fitted to each curated fish rather than to a
    zebrafish-specific one.
    doi:10.1101/2024.11.22.624881
    https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.11.22.624881

EMSC / SeismicPortal
    Earthquake catalogue for 2026-06-21, all magnitudes, via the FDSN event
    service. Curated to data/curated/quakes_21062026.json.
    The live feed also subscribes to the real-time standing-order channel,
    which pushes each event as EMSC publishes it.
    https://www.seismicportal.eu/
    https://www.seismicportal.eu/fdsnws/event/1/query
    https://www.seismicportal.eu/realtime.html

U.S. Geological Survey
    Live earthquake summary feed, polled alongside EMSC for the live quakes.
    Public domain. https://earthquake.usgs.gov/
    https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/summary/all_day.geojson

